+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of seconds,
+like `120`, or one or more groups of an integer followed by a unit: `d`
+(days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), or `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear
+at most once, in that order, like `90m`, `1h30m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Units are
+case-insensitive. Signs, decimals, and spaces are rejected. A
+{class}`~datetime.timedelta` value, like a default, is passed through as-is.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
